      "content": "A full conservation report will take months, and we'll miss the window for the Q4 cataloging. Look, I've seen these types of readings before on genuine pieces. Sometimes it's just superficial cleaning or minor localized touch-ups from the 19th century that get caught in the scan. Is it possible we're overreacting to what might just be common restoration work? Can we find a way to qualify this so it doesn't kill the whole auction?",
